cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Numerical Solutions and Stability Analysis of the Solow Growth Model: A Comparative Study of Euler and Runge-Kutta Methods"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sulyman"
    given-names: "Saleem"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sulymansaleem04-source/solow-numerical-methods"
abstract: "The Solow growth model reduces to one nonlinear differential equation for capital per effective worker. Under Cobb-Douglas production it has a closed-form solution, so the error of numerical methods can be measured exactly. This study compares the Euler, Heun and classical fourth-order Runge-Kutta methods on the model calibrated to Nigeria for 1990 to 2023, measuring accuracy and stability limits."
keywords:
  - Solow growth model
  - numerical methods
  - Euler method
  - Runge-Kutta
  - stability analysis
  - Nigeria
